rk.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Douglas Irving Ostrover | Co-Founder, Chairman & Co-CEO | Age 63 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $416K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue falling 9%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $878K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $493K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Blue Owl Capital Inc. is a large-cap financial services business with a $15.4B market cap on $568M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -25% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are expanding by +72.0pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $1.2B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 211 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 15.93\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 8.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.9% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and stock-based comp at 119% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.4\u00d7 its fair share 